A quick overview of a custom-made wooden shelf made from raw beech, to fit some space i had in my corridor.

## The motivation

I have been long willing to build something from raw wood, so when we raised the idea of filling some unused space we had in the corridor with a shelf to store kids' books, I knew it was one opportunity to seize.

Here is a photo of the final result which I am quite happy with

The shelf had to fit in alignment with a door that was encroaching on the corridor about 16cm, and below an existing recessed shelf with a frame situated at abotu 70cm above the floor.

### The design

Design : asymmetry
Height to fit the different books
Deicded to put it at floor level and not to add a ""surelevation"", originally 7 cm

